# Project Structure

Simplified medallion ETL + FastAPI catalog. See [domain-architecture.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/domain-architecture.mdc) for data flow and [tech-stack.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/tech-stack.mdc) for versions.

## Root Layout

```
binder_etl/
├── .cursor/rules/           # Architecture rules (SSOT for agents)
├── docker-compose.yaml      # MinIO + Postgres (Airflow meta) + Airflow (+ spark-dev profile)
├── .env.example
├── requirements/
│   ├── spark.txt
│   └── airflow.txt
├── airbyte/
│   └── README.md            # abctl install + TikTok connection
├── dags/
│   └── tiktok/
│       └── tiktok_daily.py  # sync_raw → bronze → silver → gold
├── src/
│   ├── config/settings.py   # MinIO (+ shared settings)
│   ├── spark_session.py     # Spark + Delta + S3A
│   ├── api/                 # FastAPI catalog app
│   │   ├── main.py          # app + async lifespan (Spark init before serve)
│   │   └── routes/
│   │       └── catalog.py   # GET catalog for backend
│   ├── io/
│   │   ├── reader.py        # Read Parquet/Delta from MinIO
│   │   └── writer.py        # Write Delta to MinIO
│   ├── pipelines/
│   │   └── run.py           # CLI: run {bronze|silver|gold} {platform}
│   └── transformers/
│       ├── base.py          # Thin shared base (one file)
│       └── tiktok/
│           ├── tables.py    # SSOT: streams, dedupe, join key contract, catalog entities
│           ├── bronze.py    # layer orchestrator (I/O + ETL_STRICT)
│           ├── silver.py
│           ├── gold.py
│           └── transforms/  # pure DataFrame logic
│               ├── silver/  # one module per stream + SILVER_TRANSFORMS registry
│               ├── gold/    # one module per fact + GOLD_TRANSFORMS registry
│               └── catalog/ # silver → catalog API row shape
├── dev/                     # Dev-only Spark sandbox (not production code)
│   ├── examples/            # Checked-in inspection templates
│   └── sandbox/             # Personal scratch scripts (gitignored)
├── infra/
│   ├── airflow/Dockerfile
│   └── spark-dev/Dockerfile # Compose profile: dev
└── tests/
    ├── test_spark_minio.py
    └── test_pipeline.py
```

**Deferred:** facts / dashboard Postgres serving (facts ⋈ Bridge); Bridge discovery CRUD on backend.

**Catalog API:** run with uvicorn against `src.api.main:app` (async lifespan initializes Spark before accept). Spark/MinIO work in handlers runs off the event loop.

## Naming Conventions

| Item | Pattern | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| Platform folder | lowercase slug | `tiktok`, `meta`, `google_ads` |
| Airflow DAG id | `{platform}_daily` | `tiktok_daily` |
| Airflow tasks | `{layer}_{platform}` | `bronze_tiktok`, `gold_tiktok` |
| Raw path | `airbyte/{platform}/{stream}/` | `airbyte/tiktok/campaigns/` |
| Delta path | `{layer}/{platform}/{table}/` | `silver/tiktok/campaigns/` |
| Pipeline CLI | `run {layer} {platform}` | `run gold tiktok` |
| Catalog API | FastAPI under `src/api/` | GET catalog endpoint(s) |
| Metadata SSOT | `src/transformers/{platform}/tables.py` | streams, dedupe, join keys, catalog |
| Silver transforms | `src/transformers/{platform}/transforms/silver/{stream}.py` | column renames + casts |
| Gold transforms | `src/transformers/{platform}/transforms/gold/{fact}.py` | joins + business grain |
| Catalog transforms | `src/transformers/{platform}/transforms/catalog/{entity}.py` | hierarchy rows for API |

## Layer vs Transform Split

| File kind | Location | Responsibility |
|-----------|----------|----------------|
| Orchestrator | `{platform}/bronze.py`, `silver.py`, `gold.py` | MinIO I/O, loop streams/facts, ETL_STRICT |
| Metadata | `{platform}/tables.py` | paths, dedupe keys, gold fact config, catalog entities, Bridge join keys |
| Transforms | `{platform}/transforms/{layer}/` | pure `DataFrame → DataFrame` (or gold/catalog: Spark + sources) |
| API | `src/api/` | FastAPI; lifespan Spark init; catalog routes call transforms |

Bronze has no transform modules — dedupe is generic via `base.dedupe()` + `tables.py` keys. Catalog is **not** a pipeline CLI layer — only API + transforms.

## Entry Points

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `src/pipelines/run.py` | CLI for bronze, silver, gold |
| `src/api/main.py` | FastAPI app; async lifespan initializes Spark before serve |
| `src/api/routes/catalog.py` | GET catalog for backend Bridge discovery |
| `src/spark_session.py` | Spark session with Delta + MinIO S3A |
| `src/transformers/{platform}/tables.py` | Platform metadata single source of truth |
| `dags/{platform}/{platform}_daily.py` | Airflow orchestration (ends at gold) |
| `dev/` + Compose `spark-dev` (profile `dev`) | Dev-only sandbox for exploring lake data / prototyping transformers |

## Add a New Platform (Checklist)

1. Create `src/transformers/{platform}/tables.py` with streams, raw paths, dedupe keys, join key contract, catalog entities
2. Implement `bronze.py`, `silver.py`, `gold.py` orchestrators extending shared `base.py`
3. Add silver transforms under `transforms/silver/`, gold under `transforms/gold/`, catalog under `transforms/catalog/`
4. Normalize silver to canonical columns: `ad_account_id`, `campaign_id`, `ad_group_id`, `ad_id` (all strings)
5. Wire catalog transforms so FastAPI can return the hierarchy contract for this platform
6. Add platform to `PLATFORMS` list in pipeline runner
7. Create `dags/{platform}/{platform}_daily.py` ending at `gold_{platform}`
8. Document Airbyte connection in `airbyte/README.md`
9. Add smoke test under `tests/`

Copy the TikTok folder pattern — do not refactor shared code unless duplication exceeds ~30 lines.

## Simplification vs binder_data_hub

| Area | binder_data_hub | binder_etl |
|------|-----------------|------------|
| Base classes | `base_bronze.py`, `base_silver.py`, `base_gold.py` | Single `base.py` |
| Pipeline CLI | `run_layer` + legacy aliases | One `run.py` (bronze/silver/gold) |
| Postgres landing | Not implemented | Deferred (facts ⋈ Bridge later) |
| Query API | Full FastAPI catalog | FastAPI catalog (MVP) |
| Docker | Multiple Dockerfiles | Shared image where possible |

`binder_data_hub` is inspiration only — do not copy its complexity.
